Cell["\<\
All symbols follow Table 2. The egg density is denoted by U and the nymph \
density by M for compatibility with Mathematica.
H represents the proportion of larvae that survive the larval stage. This \
variable simplifies the computation of the survival integral. The same \
approach is used in the Julia code for numerical simulations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.984819737459536*^9, 3.984819765428179*^9}, {
   3.984819905765223*^9, 3.984819936518158*^9}, 3.9848200288652363`*^9, {
